{"tool": "finish", "summary": "API requests that modify `users` or `feeds` rows now append to a new `audit_log` table; the build and existing tests pass (53 unit packages, 102 integration tests). Nothing exercises the new audit rows themselves \u2014 I had no way to query the table from here.\n\n**What gets logged**\n- One audit row per modified row, written in the same transaction as the change. Each row records the acting user, HTTP method and path, the table, the action (`insert`/`update`/`delete`) and the row id.\n- REST API: user create/update/delete, feed create/update/delete, single-feed refresh, OPML import, and category delete.\n- Deleting a user or a category also logs each feed removed with it. In the audited path those feeds are deleted explicitly rather than by the foreign-key cascade, so they can be recorded.\n- The last-login update during authentication is not logged, as specified.\n\n**Things you might not expect**\n- **Schema is my own guess.** The task didn't specify columns, so I chose `id, created_at, actor_user_id, request_method, request_path, table_name, action, row_id`. If the acceptance tests expect particular column names, this is where they would fail.\n- **Refresh-all and refresh-category log asynchronously.** Those endpoints queue jobs for the background workers, so the audit rows appear when each feed is actually refreshed, not before the response returns. Scheduler-triggered refreshes are not logged.\n- **Google Reader API is included.** I treated it as an API too: subscribe, unsubscribe, rename, move and disable-tag are audited. The Fever API doesn't modify either table.\n- **Web UI and CLI are not audited.** They share the same storage code but run without an audit context.\n- **Feed creation always runs in a transaction now**, including from non-API callers.\n\nThe core is in `internal/storage/audit.go` (`Storage.WithAudit`); the migration is the last entry in `internal/database/migrations.go`.", "t": 1794464252.122}
{"tool": "_result", "name": "finish", "chars": 55, "t": 1794464252.122}
